{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792947397,"nonce":"u4xwbuyLuITO8Oot7575CfVmT94=","title":"Windows: zypy generators crash (0xC0000005) since the stub interpreter","message":"CI run 40208690417 (140e0c66), native tests x86_64-pc-windows-msvc: zypy conformance exceptions/generator_raise_consumed.py, exceptions/index_error_in_loop.py and iteration/for_else.py exit -1073741819 (access violation) at their first generator. Linux, Intel macOS and arm64 macOS pass. The previous green run (40189870612) predates 893407f3.\n\nCause: collector::query_stack on Windows read GetCurrentThreadStackLimits, whose high limit is the TEB's StackBase. krio-fiber swaps StackBase/StackLimit on every fiber switch (DeallocationStack stays), so the first query made on a fiber cached (thread reservation base, fiber top). host_stack caches per thread, so from then on a mark on a fiber stack above the thread's stack counted as the thread's own stack with gigabytes of room. lazy_interpret (893407f3) then ran the HIR interpreter on the fiber's 64 KB stack, which on Windows is a heap block with no guard page.\n\nThe same range feeds the collector's dead-frame clearing (note_frame_depth, clear_dead_frames, clear_stack_below) and its host stack top.\n\nFix: on Windows the thread's stack is its reservation: the low limit is its base, and VirtualQuery walks the regions sharing that allocation base to its end, which no fiber switch changes.\n\nSeparately in the same run: async_sleep_native async_set_timeout_is_cooperative_non_blocking failed on Intel macOS with 40 ms for a call that only pushes a timer (threshold 25 ms); the timer is lengthened so the bound is half of it.","files":null}]}